# snapdragon-firewall-reconcile — RELEASE_STATE host-nftables convergence timer (60s).
#
# The TIMER half of the Layer-3 nftables backstop (the OpenRC oneshot renders +
# loads the table once at boot, BEFORE containerd/kubelet/tailscaled; this cron
# entry re-runs it every 60s so a hand-edited /etc/snapdragon/release-state or a
# freshly-written /etc/snapdragon/go-live marker — the future go-live wizard's
# LIVE-device flip — takes effect without a reboot/reflash). cronie reads
# /etc/cron.d (the same mechanism the device-registry/vpn/policy syncs use).
# DEFAULT-ON: baked + activated UNCONDITIONALLY (core hardening, not an
# optional service), unlike the STAGED vpn/tor/domain reconcile crons which
# only land in /etc/cron.d on selection.
#
# The reconcile is idempotent + FAIL-CLOSED: a read/render/apply error leaves
# the existing (safe, INTERNAL-by-default) ruleset in place.
#
# Field order: min hour dom month dow user command
* * * * * root /usr/sbin/snapdragon-firewall-reconcile >> /var/log/snapdragon-firewall-reconcile.log 2>&1
